  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Find the mean and standard deviation of each set of data. Give standard deviations correct to two decimal places.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p24-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$5,\\ 6,\\ 6,\\ 7,\\ 8,\\ 9,\\ 22$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\overline{x}=9$, $\\sigma\\approx5.45$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\overline{x}&=\\frac{5+6+6+7+8+9+22}{7}\\\\\\overline{x}&=9\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sigma^2&=\\frac{(5-9)^2+(6-9)^2+(6-9)^2+(7-9)^2+(8-9)^2+(9-9)^2+(22-9)^2}{7}\\\\\\sigma^2&=\\frac{16+9+9+4+1+0+169}{7}\\\\\\sigma^2&=\\frac{208}{7}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sigma&=\\sqrt{\\frac{208}{7}}\\\\\\sigma&\\approx5.45\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$11,\\ 7,\\ 8,\\ 9,\\ 8,\\ 10,\\ 10$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\overline{x}=9$, $\\sigma\\approx1.31$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\overline{x}&=\\frac{11+7+8+9+8+10+10}{7}\\\\\\overline{x}&=9\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sigma^2&=\\frac{(11-9)^2+(7-9)^2+(8-9)^2+(9-9)^2+(8-9)^2+(10-9)^2+(10-9)^2}{7}\\\\\\sigma^2&=\\frac{4+4+1+0+1+1+1}{7}\\\\\\sigma^2&=\\frac{12}{7}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sigma&=\\sqrt{\\frac{12}{7}}\\\\\\sigma&\\approx1.31\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$1,\\ 3,\\ 7,\\ 9,\\ 11,\\ 15,\\ 17$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\overline{x}=9$, $\\sigma\\approx5.45$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\overline{x}&=\\frac{1+3+7+9+11+15+17}{7}\\\\\\overline{x}&=9\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sigma^2&=\\frac{(1-9)^2+(3-9)^2+(7-9)^2+(9-9)^2+(11-9)^2+(15-9)^2+(17-9)^2}{7}\\\\\\sigma^2&=\\frac{64+36+4+0+4+36+64}{7}\\\\\\sigma^2&=\\frac{208}{7}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sigma&=\\sqrt{\\frac{208}{7}}\\\\\\sigma&\\approx5.45\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Compare the sets of data using their means and standard deviations.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "All three sets have mean $9$. Set b has the smallest standard deviation and is less spread out. Sets a and c have the same standard deviation, although their distributions differ.",
          "worked": "All three means are $9$, so the sets have the same centre as measured by the mean.\n\nSet b has standard deviation approximately $1.31$, compared with approximately $5.45$ for both a and c, so b is less spread out about its mean.\n\nSets a and c have equal standard deviations, but a has an isolated high value, $22$, whereas c is symmetric about $9$. Equal means and standard deviations do not imply identical distributions.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      }
    ]
